# Everything at once on an announcing mesh of 121 radios: a ground station, drones 1 to 119 reporting every second,
# radio 120 empty until it comes up as a clone of drone-5 at 10 s beside the original. Radios 101 to 103 flood gcs's
# name with 20 000 junk wires a second each from 2 s to 32 s; drone-104 holds the key and spams nav at 100 a second for
# a second with a lying clock; radio 110 replays the last wire it heard at 20 s; radio 111 is a relay that holds the
# first 4 s of wires for a week. The clone's reports are believed while an honest report of the older epoch could still
# arrive (600 s). At 35 s the clock jumps a week: the held calls come back as Replay where gcs is known, the clone's
# epoch is below the floor, and three more reports land. No noise: a receiver's bit flips touch
# nothing else (noisy-radio), and a flipped version byte is one log a cipher for the same run.
